// Sandbox Gateway <-> `modbit-guest` wire protocol (M8.3; docs/21 "Sandbox
// substrate boundary", "`modbit-guest`"; docs/33 "Sandbox Gateway"; docs/30
// "Version compatibility": guest and gateway negotiate their method set
// before a sandbox is admitted). Same length-prefixed framing as the local
// SurfaceProtocol, carried on the substrate's private channel (vsock into a
// MicroVM, a Unix socket for the reference backend). The guest never decides
// policy: it enforces the policy the gateway admitted it with and refuses
// everything else. Every call after admission is authenticated with the
// ephemeral credential the gateway issued (an HMAC over the call), so a
// frame that did not come from the gateway that admitted the guest is
// refused, and every call names the task, effect and capability it acts
// under (REQ-EV-0289).

